{"name":"Holland Tulip","hex":"#f89851","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holland","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of linen cloth, originally from Holland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holland"},{"term":"tulip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of flowering plant, genus Tulipa.","The flower of this plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tulip"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holland","blocks":[{"text":"Holland is a geographical region and former province on the western coast of the Netherlands. From the 10th to the 16th century, Holland proper was a unified political region within the Holy Roman Empire as a county ruled by the counts of Holland. By the 17th century, the province of Holland had risen to become a maritime and economic power, dominating the other provinces of the newly independent Dutch Republic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Holland_position.svg/330px-Holland_position.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holland","wikidata":"Q102911"},{"title":"Tulip","blocks":[{"text":"Tulips are spring-blooming perennial herbaceous bulbiferous geophytes in the Tulipa genus. Their flowers are usually large, showy, and brightly coloured, generally red, orange, pink, yellow, or white. They often have a different coloured blotch at the base of the tepals, internally. Because of a degree of variability within the populations and a long history of cultivation, classification has been complex and controversial. The tulip is a member of the lily family, Liliaceae, along with 14 other genera, where it is most closely related to Amana, Erythronium, and Gagea in the tribe Lilieae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/%D7%A6%D7%91%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%9D.JPG/330px-%D7%A6%D7%91%D7%A2%D7%95%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%9D.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulip","wikidata":"Q93201"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Netherlands_Density.png/500px-Netherlands_Density.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Netherlands_Density.png/500px-Netherlands_Density.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Netherlands by population density by province (2006)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANetherlands_Density.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/500px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/1280px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg/500px-COMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of Holland (1682)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOMITATUS_HOLLANDIAE_1682.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif/500px-Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif/500px-Provincie_Noord-Holland.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Holland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProvincie_Noord-Holland.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Provincie_Zuid-Holland.gif/500px-Provincie_Zuid-Holland.gif?utm_source=en.w